# Independent shoulder reference: local-only source notice

Source: OSEL-DAM / U.S. Food and Drug Administration,
[ShoulderFiniteElementModel, pinned commit](https://github.com/OSEL-DAM/ShoulderFiniteElementModel/tree/fc9f3e56b104c06759750495be1f8dd5d53c1741).
The source LICENSE and publisher notes declare CC0-1.0; source LICENSE SHA-256 is
`a2010f343487d3f7618affe54f789f5487602331c0a8d03f49e9a7c547cf0499`.
The exact licence, publisher notes, input inventory and conversion/readback evidence
are retained in the Atlas source/quarantine checkpoints. No proprietary solver,
texture, font, new dependency, paid dataset or new service is required for this path.

Six derived parts remain an unvalidated, independent, unitless draft. CC0 does not
constitute anatomical/clinical validation, patient privacy/release clearance, FDA
endorsement, device qualification, or a guarantee of fitness for medical use. Source
scientific limitations remain. Constructed cartilage provenance and the excluded
Gcart topology hold must accompany any later approved presentation.

This Website change contains the private transport and generated local metadata.
The actual catalogue/GLB objects are staged outside public assets and remain F-only.
No object is uploaded by these scripts, no learner inventory entry is added, and no
remote use is enabled. Source-only recovery deliberately excludes geometry, catalogue,
generated registry, emulator state, scans, private decisions and runtime evidence.
Existing dependency/font/asset notices and product access policies remain in force.
